  "conclusion": "Growing only the three mixed depth-two leaves raises hard held-out entropy reduction from 42.84% to 55.61%, a 22.34% reduction of the impurity remaining after depth two. Leaves 0 and 2 provide strong local held-out gains of 33.40% and 27.70%; leaf 1 provides a weaker but positive 6.37%. All ten digits retain the same majority final leaf between train and test, and leaf label distributions differ by at most 4.79% total variation. The result supports greedy independent growth with a minimum held-out local-gain threshold; the digit-1 terminal remains unsplit."
